      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="introduction">
        <tei:p>The following love poem is one of the Seliḥot recited between Rosh Hashanah and Yom Kippur. Ibn Gayat (1038 – 1089) was not timid about using the most intimate symbols in asking God to become reconciled with us.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_17543_introduction"/>
